== Tortilla Strips ==

Preheat a #pan{} with @olive oil{1/4%cup} over medium-high heat. Cut @corn tortillas{8}(into thin strips) and fry them in batches in the hot oil until crisp. Remove from the pan and allow them to drain on a paper towel. Repeat with remaining tortilla strips, adding more oil as needed then set aside.


== Chicken Tortilla Soup ==

Preheat a #pot{} or #dutch oven{} with @light olive oil{2%Tbsp} over medium-high heat. Add @yellow onion{1}(chopped), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), and @jalapeno peppers{1-2}(seeded and diced) and sauté until veggies soften.

Add @chicken broth{32%oz}, @crushed tomatoes{28%can}, @chicken breasts{1%lb}((2 medium), or leftover rotisserie chicken*), @corn{15%oz can}(drained and rinsed), @black beans{15%oz can}(drained and rinsed), @chili powder{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1 1/2%tsp}, and @salt{to taste}. Bring to a boil and let simmer for about ~{20%minutes} or until chicken is just cooked through and easy to shred.

Remove chicken from the pot and shred it using 2 forks. Add shredded chicken back to the soup and simmer another ~{5%minutes}. Remove from heat and stir in @cilantro{1/3%cup}(chopped, plus more to garnish) and @lime juice{1 1/2%Tbsp}(from 1 lime, or to taste).

Serve the soup garnished with some tortilla strips, @avocado{1}(diced), fresh cilantro, and @lime{1}(cut into wedges, to serve), or use your favorite toppings.

